   "text": "I read the drawing as a symmetric dimer: two identical bicyclic cores joined through a central diyne linker. Each half is an N-methyl-L-alanine amide on a thiazepane\u2013pyrrolidine bicycle carrying two allyl groups. The bicycle's carboxamide is attached to an aminoindanyl ether.\n\n**Left half**\n- The N-methylalanine NH\u2013CH(CH3)\u2013C(=O) unit has a hashed methyl, which gives L-configuration.\n- The bicycle is a 7-membered ring containing S, fused to a 5-membered ring containing N.\n- The quaternary ring carbon carries two allyl groups.\n- The ring-fusion carbon (the one bearing H) has a hashed H.\n- The carbon bearing the NH\u2013Ala group has a wedged N, and the carbon bearing the carboxamide has a wedged C(=O).\n- The indane carbon bonded to the amide N has a hashed N. The adjacent indane carbon has a hashed O.\n\n**Linker**\n- The two indane oxygens are joined by \u2013O\u2013CH2\u2013C\u2261C\u2013C\u2261C\u2013CH2\u2013O\u2013.\n\n**Right half**\n- This is the left half rotated by 180\u00b0 (C2 symmetry), so I wrote it in reverse order and re-derived each @/@@ by permuting the neighbour order of the left-half centres.\n\nI assigned each stereocentre from the wedge and hash bonds and checked that the SMILES is valid and matches the drawing atom for atom.\n\nSMILES: CN[C@@H](C)C(=O)N[C@H]1CCS[C@H]2CC(CC=C)(CC=C)[C@@H](C(=O)N[C@H]3c4ccccc4C[C@H]3OCC#CC#CCO[C@@H]3Cc4ccccc4[C@@H]3NC(=O)[C@H]5N6C(=O)[C@@H](NC(=O)[C@H](C)NC)CCS[C@H]6CC5(CC=C)CC=C)N2C1=O"
